IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgba-nouns`

-- INSTRUMENT: Broadcasting (Television and Radio Licensing) (Amendment) Regulations 2004 (S 333/2004), made under s 66 of the Act by the Media Development Authority of Singapore with the Minister's approval.
-- Deposit: ../../../broadcasting-television-and-radio-licensing-amendment-regulations-2004/registers/source-bundle/BA1994-S333-2004.txt (e-Gazette PDF, pdftotext -layout, unedited).
-- First published in the Government Gazette on 15 June 2004 at 5:00 pm, made 11 June 2004, "shall come into operation on 21st June 2004" (paragraph 1).
-- It amends Rg 1 (2004 Ed.), encoded in `sgba-i-rg1.l4`. Only the REPLACEMENT or NEW text is a rule here: a regulation it deletes is a deletion (the version table of `sgba-versions.l4` records which regulations the amended Regulations have),
-- and a regulation that it amends by deleting words is restated in full in its amended form where the amended form is a rule the person meets.
-- Nothing in this module rebuilds the amended Regulations from anything but the words the Regulations 2004 print; where the amended form is not printed whole, the module says how it was assembled.

§ `Paragraph 1: commencement, as the version row`

-- src:3 | First published in the Government Gazette, Electronic Edition, on 15th June 2004 at 5:00 pm.
-- src:20 | Citation and commencement
-- src:21 | 1. These Regulations may be cited as the Broadcasting (Television
-- src:22 | and Radio Licensing) (Amendment) Regulations 2004 and shall
-- src:23 | come into operation on 21st June 2004.
@ref S 333/2004 publication line and para 1 (citation and commencement) (src:3-23)
-- Two dates: it takes effect on 21 June 2004 ("shall come into operation on 21st June 2004") and was published on 15 June 2004 (5:00 pm; the time is not kept).
`Rg 1 as amended by S 333/2004` MEANS
    `Rg 1 version` WITH `source` IS "S 333/2004, made 11 June 2004, first published 15 June 2004 at 5:00 pm, in operation from 21 June 2004"
                      , `the text read` IS "amended by S 333/2004"
                      , `takes effect on` IS (Date 21 6 2004)
                      , `published on` IS (Date 15 6 2004)
                      , `the Regulations are in force` IS TRUE

§ `Paragraph 2: regulation 2 (definitions) amended`

-- src:25 | Amendment of regulation 2
-- src:26 | 2. Regulation 2 of the Broadcasting (Television and Radio
-- src:28 | Regulations as the principal Regulations) is amended —
-- src:29 | (a) by deleting the definitions of ‘‘broadcast sound receiver’’
-- src:30 | and ‘‘broadcast television receiver’’ in paragraph (1) and
-- src:31 | substituting the following definitions:
-- src:32 | ‘‘ ‘‘broadcasting apparatus’’ means any broadcast sound
-- src:33 | receiver or broadcast television receiver;
-- src:34 | ‘‘commercial property’’ means any premises or any part
-- src:35 | thereof which —
-- src:36 | (a) are permitted to be used pursuant to any
-- src:37 | other written law wholly or partly for the
-- src:38 | purpose of any business or are lawfully so
-- src:39 | used; or
-- src:40 | (b) are occupied by any charity,
-- src:41 | but does not include any hotel, hospital or institution
-- src:42 | providing education or instruction;
-- src:45 | ‘‘hospital’’ includes a private hospital as defined in
-- src:46 | the Private Hospitals and Medical Clinics Act
-- src:47 | (Cap. 248);’’;
-- src:48 | (b) by deleting the definition of ‘‘Television Receive-Only
-- src:49 | Satellite Receiving System’’ or ‘‘TVRO system’’ in
-- src:50 | paragraph (1) and substituting the following definition:
-- src:51 | ‘‘ ‘‘licence’’ means any licence granted under section 20 of
-- src:52 | the Act in respect of any broadcasting apparatus;’’;
-- src:53 | and
-- src:54 | (c) by deleting paragraph (2).
@ref S 333/2004 para 2, reg 2 as amended: "broadcasting apparatus", "commercial property", "hospital", "licence" (src:25-54)
-- The definitions of "broadcast sound receiver" and "broadcast television receiver" and of "TVRO system", and paragraph (2), are deleted and not replaced: as amended the Regulations use "broadcast sound receiver" and "broadcast television receiver" without defining them
-- (the Act's First Schedule defines them "for the purposes of this Schedule"; fork F-BA-11 in NOTES.md). The receiving facts are taken as the same facts as in the Revised Edition.
GIVEN `it is a broadcast sound receiver` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a broadcast television receiver` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 2(1) the apparatus is broadcasting apparatus (S 333/2004)` MEANS
    `it is a broadcast sound receiver` OR `it is a broadcast television receiver`

GIVEN `the premises are permitted to be used under another written law wholly or partly for the purpose of a business, or are lawfully so used` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the premises are occupied by a charity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the premises are a hotel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the premises are a hospital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the premises are an institution providing education or instruction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 2(1) the premises are a commercial property (S 333/2004)` MEANS
    (`the premises are permitted to be used under another written law wholly or partly for the purpose of a business, or are lawfully so used` OR `the premises are occupied by a charity`) AND (NOT (`the premises are a hotel` OR `the premises are a hospital` OR `the premises are an institution providing education or instruction`))

GIVEN `it is a hospital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a private hospital as defined in the Private Hospitals and Medical Clinics Act (Cap. 248)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 2(1) the premises are a hospital (S 333/2004)` MEANS
    `it is a hospital` OR `it is a private hospital as defined in the Private Hospitals and Medical Clinics Act (Cap. 248)`

GIVEN `it is a licence granted under section 20 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in respect of broadcasting apparatus` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 2(1) the licence is a licence within these Regulations (S 333/2004)` MEANS
    `it is a licence granted under section 20 of the Act` AND `it is in respect of broadcasting apparatus`

§ `Paragraph 4: regulation 5 (duration of and fee for licence) amended`

-- src:59 | Amendment of regulation 5
-- src:60 | 4. Regulation 5 of the principal Regulations is amended —
-- src:61 | (a) by deleting paragraphs (2) and (3) and substituting the
-- src:62 | following paragraph:
-- src:63 | ‘‘(2) Subject to regulation 37 (1), a licence shall be
-- src:64 | valid for such period as the Authority may determine
-- src:65 | unless it is sooner determined in accordance with these
-- src:66 | Regulations.’’;
-- src:67 | (b) by deleting paragraph (6) and substituting the following
-- src:68 | paragraph:
-- src:69 | ‘‘(6) The additional fee referred to in paragraph (5)
-- src:70 | is —
-- src:71 | (a) $13 for varying to a licence in item 3 of the First
-- src:72 | Schedule; and
-- src:73 | (b) $83 for varying to a licence in item 4 of the First
-- src:74 | Schedule.’’; and
-- src:75 | (c) by deleting paragraph (8) and substituting the following
-- src:76 | paragraph:
-- src:77 | ‘‘(8) The additional fee referred to in paragraph (7)
-- src:78 | is —
-- src:79 | (a) $52.50 for varying to a licence in item 6 of the
-- src:80 | First Schedule;
-- src:83 | (b) $35 for varying to a licence in item 8 of the First
-- src:84 | Schedule; and
-- src:85 | (c) $70 for all other cases.’’.
@ref S 333/2004 para 4: reg 5(2) substituted; reg 5(6) and (8) substituted (src:59-85)
-- The Revised Edition's reg 5(3) (a sound receiver licence for a vehicle valid from the date of issue) is deleted with reg 5(2); the licence is valid for the period the Authority determines.
GIVEN `the Authority determined a period for the licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licence has been sooner determined in accordance with the Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 5(2) the licence is valid for the period the Authority determined (S 333/2004)` MEANS
    `the Authority determined a period for the licence` AND (NOT `the licence has been sooner determined in accordance with the Regulations`)

GIVEN `the item of the First Schedule the licence is varied to` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Rg 1 reg 5(6) the additional fee for varying a sound receiver licence (S 333/2004)` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the item of the First Schedule the licence is varied to` EQUALS 3 THEN JUST 13
           IF ^ EQUALS 4 THEN JUST 83
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN `the item of the First Schedule the licence is varied to` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Rg 1 reg 5(8) the additional fee for varying a monochrome licence to a colour licence (S 333/2004)` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the item of the First Schedule the licence is varied to` EQUALS 6 THEN 52.5
           IF ^ EQUALS 8 THEN 35
           OTHERWISE 70

§ `Paragraphs 5 to 7: regulations 6, 7 and 8 amended`

-- src:87 | Amendment of regulation 6
-- src:88 | 5. Regulation 6 of the principal Regulations is amended by
-- src:89 | deleting the words ‘‘for a broadcast sound receiver or a broadcast
-- src:90 | television receiver’’.
@ref S 333/2004 para 5: reg 6 (late payment fee) now covers every licence (src:87-90)
GIVEN `the licence is of the kind a Second Schedule item names` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 6 a late payment fee is payable in accordance with the Second Schedule (S 333/2004)` MEANS
    `the licence is of the kind a Second Schedule item names`

-- src:96 | Amendment of regulation 8
-- src:97 | 7. Regulation 8 of the principal Regulations is amended by
-- src:98 | deleting the words ‘‘for any broadcast sound receiver or any
-- src:99 | broadcast television receiver’’.
@ref S 333/2004 para 7: reg 8 (fee waiver) no longer confined to a sound or television receiver licence (src:96-99)
GIVEN `the person is required to use the person's broadcasting apparatus for Government purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is blind and the fee is for operating a broadcast sound receiver` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is deaf and the fee is for operating a broadcast television receiver` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the circumstances appear to the Authority to be reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 8 the case is within the Authority's discretion to waive or reduce the fee (S 333/2004)` MEANS
    `the person is required to use the person's broadcasting apparatus for Government purposes` OR `the person is blind and the fee is for operating a broadcast sound receiver` OR `the person is deaf and the fee is for operating a broadcast television receiver` OR `the circumstances appear to the Authority to be reasonable`

§ `Paragraph 9: regulation 15 (information) substituted`

-- src:104 | Deletion and substitution of regulation 15
-- src:105 | 9. Regulation 15 of the principal Regulations is deleted and the
-- src:106 | following regulation substituted therefor:
-- src:107 | ‘‘Information
-- src:108 | 15. Any person shall, if so required by the Authority by notice
-- src:109 | in writing, furnish within a reasonable time such information as
-- src:110 | the Authority considers necessary for the purposes of the Act or
-- src:111 | these Regulations, being information within the possession of
-- src:112 | that person.’’.
@ref S 333/2004 para 9: reg 15 substituted (src:104-112)
GIVEN `the Authority has required the person by notice in writing to furnish information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority considers the information necessary for the purposes of the Act or these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is within the possession of that person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 15 the person must furnish the information within a reasonable time (S 333/2004)` MEANS
    `the Authority has required the person by notice in writing to furnish information` AND `the Authority considers the information necessary for the purposes of the Act or these Regulations` AND `the information is within the possession of that person`

§ `Paragraph 10: regulations 16 to 22 deleted; new regulation 16`

-- src:115 | Deletion of regulations 16 to 22 and new regulation 16
-- src:116 | 10. Regulations 16 to 22 of the principal Regulations are deleted
-- src:117 | and the following regulation substituted therefor:
-- src:118 | ‘‘Application for dealers’ licence
-- src:119 | 16. An application for a licence to import, offer for sale, sell or
-- src:120 | otherwise deal in any broadcasting apparatus shall be made to
-- src:121 | the Authority in writing.’’.
@ref S 333/2004 para 10: new reg 16 (application for a dealer's licence) (src:115-121)
GIVEN `the application for a licence to import, offer for sale, sell or otherwise deal in broadcasting apparatus is made to the Authority in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 16 the application is as the regulation requires (S 333/2004)` MEANS
    `the application for a licence to import, offer for sale, sell or otherwise deal in broadcasting apparatus is made to the Authority in writing`

§ `Paragraph 11: regulation 23 (broadcast sound receivers) amended`

-- src:123 | Amendment of regulation 23
-- src:124 | 11. Regulation 23 of the principal Regulations is amended —
-- src:125 | (a) by deleting paragraphs (1) and (2) and substituting the
-- src:126 | following paragraphs:
-- src:127 | ‘‘(1) An application for a licence to install or operate a
-- src:128 | broadcast sound receiver may be made at any post office
-- src:129 | or at such other places as the Authority may require.
-- src:130 | (2) A licence shall be required for every broadcast
-- src:131 | sound receiver in a vessel in respect of which a ship
-- src:132 | station licence has not been granted under the Telecom-
-- src:133 | munications Act (Cap. 323).’’; and
-- src:134 | (b) by deleting the words ‘‘, other than one which is merely
-- src:135 | carried in a vehicle or vessel,’’ in paragraph (5).
@ref S 333/2004 para 11: reg 23(1) and (2) substituted; reg 23(5) amended (src:123-135)
-- Amended reg 23(2): "A licence shall be required for every broadcast sound receiver in a vessel in respect of which a ship station licence has not been granted". The vehicle is gone from the requirement.
-- Amended reg 23(5): the words ", other than one which is merely carried in a vehicle or vessel," are deleted, so a receiver affixed by brackets or other mountings, temporarily or permanently, is deemed installed.
GIVEN `the receiver is affixed in the vehicle or vessel by brackets or other mountings, temporarily or permanently` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 23(5) the broadcast sound receiver is deemed installed (S 333/2004)` MEANS
    `the receiver is affixed in the vehicle or vessel by brackets or other mountings, temporarily or permanently`

GIVEN `the receiver is in a vessel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a ship station licence has been granted for the vessel under the Telecommunications Act (Cap. 323)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 23(2) a licence is required for the broadcast sound receiver (S 333/2004)` MEANS
    `the receiver is in a vessel` AND (NOT `a ship station licence has been granted for the vessel under the Telecommunications Act (Cap. 323)`)

GIVEN `the application is made at a post office or at another place the Authority requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 23(1) the application for a licence to install or operate a broadcast sound receiver is made as the regulation provides (S 333/2004)` MEANS
    `the application is made at a post office or at another place the Authority requires`

§ `Paragraphs 12 and 13: regulations 27 and 28 amended`

-- src:137 | Amendment of regulation 27
-- src:138 | 12. Regulation 27 of the principal Regulations is amended —
-- src:139 | (a) by deleting paragraphs (1) and (2) and substituting the
-- src:140 | following paragraph:
-- src:141 | ‘‘(1) An application for a licence to install or operate
-- src:142 | a broadcast television receiver may be made at any post
-- src:143 | office or at such other places as the Authority may
-- src:144 | require.’’; and
-- src:145 | (b) by deleting the words ‘‘used by’’ in paragraph (4) and
-- src:146 | substituting the words ‘‘installed or operated by’’.
@ref S 333/2004 para 12: reg 27(1) and (2) substituted by an application provision; reg 27(4) amended (src:137-146)
-- The Revised Edition's reg 27(1) ("No person shall operate a broadcast television receiver without a licence") is deleted and not replaced by any prohibition: the new reg 27(1) says where an application may be made.
GIVEN `the application is made at a post office or at another place the Authority requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 27(1) the application for a licence to install or operate a broadcast television receiver is made as the regulation provides (S 333/2004)` MEANS
    `the application is made at a post office or at another place the Authority requires`

GIVEN `the receiver is installed or operated by a lodger, boarder, resident guest or a person occupying a portion of the premises under a separate tenancy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 27(4) a separate licence is required (S 333/2004)` MEANS
    `the receiver is installed or operated by a lodger, boarder, resident guest or a person occupying a portion of the premises under a separate tenancy`

-- src:149 | Amendment of regulation 28
-- src:150 | 13. Regulation 28 of the principal Regulations is amended —
-- src:151 | (a) by deleting paragraph (1) and substituting the following
-- src:152 | paragraph:
-- src:153 | ‘‘(1) If the owner of the vehicle or vessel wishes to
-- src:154 | mount a broadcast television receiver in the vehicle or
-- src:155 | vessel, he shall ensure that the receiver is so mounted
-- src:156 | that it is not possible for the viewing screen to be seen
-- src:157 | from the normal driving position or from the helmsman’s
-- src:158 | position.’’; and
-- src:159 | (b) by deleting the words ‘‘, other than one which is merely
-- src:160 | carried in a vehicle or vessel,’’ in paragraph (5).
@ref S 333/2004 para 13: reg 28(1) substituted; reg 28(5) amended (src:149-160)
GIVEN `the owner of the vehicle or vessel wishes to mount a broadcast television receiver in it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the viewing screen can be seen from the normal driving position or from the helmsman's position` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 28(1) the owner has mounted the receiver as the regulation requires (S 333/2004)` MEANS
    (NOT `the owner of the vehicle or vessel wishes to mount a broadcast television receiver in it`) OR (NOT `the viewing screen can be seen from the normal driving position or from the helmsman's position`)

GIVEN `the receiver is affixed in the vehicle or vessel by brackets or other mountings, temporarily or permanently` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 28(5) the broadcast television receiver is deemed installed (S 333/2004)` MEANS
    `the receiver is affixed in the vehicle or vessel by brackets or other mountings, temporarily or permanently`

§ `Paragraph 14: new regulation 29A (commercial properties)`

-- src:162 | New regulation 29A
-- src:163 | 14. The principal Regulations are amended by inserting,
-- src:164 | immediately after regulation 29, the following regulation:
-- src:165 | ‘‘Broadcast television receivers in commercial properties
-- src:166 | 29A.—(1) A separate licence shall be required for every
-- src:167 | broadcast television receiver installed in a commercial property.
-- src:168 | (2) A licence under paragraph (1) shall permit the use of one
-- src:169 | or more broadcast sound receivers.’’.
@ref S 333/2004 para 14: new reg 29A (src:162-169)
GIVEN `the receiver is installed in a commercial property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 29A(1) a separate licence is required for the broadcast television receiver (S 333/2004)` MEANS
    `the receiver is installed in a commercial property`

GIVEN `the licence is under regulation 29A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 29A(2) the licence permits the use of one or more broadcast sound receivers (S 333/2004)` MEANS
    `the licence is under regulation 29A(1)`

§ `Paragraphs 15 to 17: regulations 31, 32 and 33 amended`

-- src:171 | Amendment of regulation 31
-- src:172 | 15. Regulation 31 of the principal Regulations is amended —
-- src:173 | (a) by deleting the words ‘‘and for every extension from that
-- src:174 | broadcast television receiver’’ in paragraph (1) (a); and
-- src:175 | (b) by deleting the words ‘‘paragraph (1) (a)’’ in paragraph (2)
-- src:176 | and substituting the words ‘‘paragraph (1)’’.
@ref S 333/2004 para 15: reg 31 amended (extensions no longer need a licence of their own) (src:171-176)
GIVEN `the receiver is installed in a hospital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the receiver is used by a member of the staff in residential quarters` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 31(1) a separate licence is required for the receiver (S 333/2004)` MEANS
    `the receiver is installed in a hospital` OR `the receiver is used by a member of the staff in residential quarters`

GIVEN `the licence is under regulation 31(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 31(2) the licence permits the use of one or more broadcast sound receivers (S 333/2004)` MEANS
    `the licence is under regulation 31(1)`

-- src:183 | Deletion and substitution of regulation 33
-- src:184 | 17. Regulation 33 of the principal Regulations is deleted and the
-- src:185 | following regulation substituted therefor:
-- src:186 | ‘‘Restricted monochrome licence
-- src:187 | 33. A licence to install or operate a broadcast television
-- src:188 | receiver in monochrome shall not be regarded as permitting the
-- src:189 | installation or operation of any broadcast television receiver in
-- src:190 | colour.’’.
@ref S 333/2004 para 17: reg 33 substituted (src:183-190)
GIVEN `the licence is to install or operate a broadcast television receiver in monochrome` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the receiver is installed or operated in colour` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 33 the licence is regarded as permitting the installation or operation (S 333/2004)` MEANS
    NOT (`the licence is to install or operate a broadcast television receiver in monochrome` AND `the receiver is installed or operated in colour`)

§ `Paragraphs 19 and 20: regulations 36 and 37 amended`

-- src:198 | Deletion and substitution of regulation 36
-- src:199 | 19. Regulation 36 of the principal Regulations is deleted and the
-- src:200 | following regulation substituted therefor:
-- src:201 | ‘‘Block licence
-- src:202 | 36. Notwithstanding the provisions of Parts IV and V, the
-- src:203 | Authority may permit —
-- src:204 | (a) the owner of a hotel or hospital to apply for a block
-- src:205 | licence for all the broadcast television receivers
-- src:206 | installed or operated within the hotel or hospital, as the
-- src:207 | case may be; and
-- src:208 | (b) the owner or occupier of any commercial property to
-- src:209 | apply for a block licence for all the broadcast television
-- src:210 | receivers installed or operated within the commercial
-- src:211 | property.’’.
@ref S 333/2004 para 19: reg 36 substituted (src:198-211)
GIVEN `the person is the owner of a hotel or hospital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the owner or occupier of a commercial property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority permits the person to apply for a block licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 36 the person may apply for a block licence for all the broadcast television receivers installed or operated within the premises (S 333/2004)` MEANS
    (`the person is the owner of a hotel or hospital` OR `the person is the owner or occupier of a commercial property`) AND `the Authority permits the person to apply for a block licence`

-- src:213 | Amendment of regulation 37
-- src:214 | 20. Regulation 37 (1) of the principal Regulations is amended
-- src:215 | by deleting the words ‘‘or hospital’’ and substituting the words
-- src:216 | ‘‘, hospital or commercial property’’.
@ref S 333/2004 para 20: reg 37(1) amended (src:213-216)
GIVEN `the licences of the receivers in a hotel, hospital or commercial property have different expiry dates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 1 reg 37(1) the Authority may vary the expiry dates to one common expiry date in issuing a block licence (S 333/2004)` MEANS
    `the licences of the receivers in a hotel, hospital or commercial property have different expiry dates`

§ `Paragraph 23: the Second Schedule substituted`

-- src:233 | Deletion and substitution of Second Schedule
-- src:234 | 23. The Second Schedule to the principal Regulations is deleted
-- src:235 | and the following Schedule substituted therefor:
-- src:237 | ‘‘SECOND SCHEDULE
-- src:238 | Regulation 6
-- src:240 | LATE PAYMENT FEES
-- src:242 | 1. Late payment fee for the grant or renewal of $10.
-- src:243 | a broadcast sound receiver licence
-- src:244 | 2. Late payment fee for the grant or renewal of $25.
-- src:245 | a broadcast television receiver licence
-- src:246 | 3. Late payment fee for the grant or renewal of $25 per broadcast
-- src:247 | a block licence television receiver.
-- src:248 | 4. Late payment fee for the grant or renewal of $75.’’.
-- src:249 | a licence to deal in broadcasting apparatus
@ref S 333/2004 para 23: Second Schedule (late payment fees) substituted (src:233-249)
-- Item 1 $10 (sound receiver licence); item 2 $25 (television receiver licence); item 3 $25 per broadcast television receiver (block licence); item 4 $75 (licence to deal in broadcasting apparatus).
-- The substituted Schedule prints no "21 days" condition, which the Revised Edition's Schedule printed in each of its two items (reading note R-4 in NOTES.md): the fee is the printed sum, and the condition is not carried.
GIVEN `the item of the Second Schedule` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of broadcast television receivers under the block licence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Rg 1 Second Schedule the late payment fee for the item (S 333/2004)` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the item of the Second Schedule` EQUALS 1 THEN JUST 10
           IF ^ EQUALS 2 THEN JUST 25
           IF ^ EQUALS 3 THEN JUST (25 TIMES `the number of broadcast television receivers under the block licence`)
           IF ^ EQUALS 4 THEN JUST 75
           OTHERWISE NOTHING
